  #   * confidential-client authentication — `token_endpoint_auth_method` on
  #     clients. Existing rows default to 'none' (public / PKCE), so no already-
  #     registered client is suddenly required to send a secret — a client opts
  #     into confidential auth explicitly at (re-)registration.
  #   * refresh-token reuse detection — `family_id` groups a rotation chain and
  #     `revoked_at` marks a consumed token, so replaying a rotated token is
  #     detected and the whole family is revoked.
